					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>CCI_REF</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-000133</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STATUS>NotAFinding</STATUS>
				<FINDING_DETAILS>MITIGATED. Attribution behind the proxy is a JOIN, not a header. Boundary's hop is a TCP session, so no HTTP proxy exists to insert X-Forwarded-For and ClientHost is the egress worker for every analyst. The ingress record carries StartUTC and ClientHost; the broker's session record carries the real client address for that window, and the two join on time and session. The ingress also captures X-Forwarded-For when present, so a future HTTP proxy in front would be recorded directly.

Evidence: traefik/traefik.yml (accessLog.fields.headers), backend/cases/brokeredsessions.py

Verified by: test/uat_srg_webtier.sh — the test drives a request through the brokered listener, then asserts the ingress record carries the join keys and the session reports the real client address</FINDING_DETAILS>
				<COMMENTS>Determination: Mitigated. Tracked in artifacts/srg_status.yml; regenerate with gen_srg_tracker.py.</COMMENTS>
				<SEVERITY_OVERRIDE />
				<SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION />
