					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>TargetKey</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA />
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIG_UUID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>24c0e41e-1385-59de-8d1a-906595a01495</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>CCI_REF</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-000803</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STATUS>Open</STATUS>
				<FINDING_DETAILS>PLANNED — requires an architectural or web-tier redesign.

FIPS 140-2/140-3 validated modules. The images use their distributions' stock OpenSSL/Go crypto, which is not a validated module — this needs FIPS-mode base images and a validated provider across Traefik, oauth2-proxy, nginx, Keycloak and Python. It is a rebuild of the web tier's runtime, not a setting.

Where: FIPS track — every web-tier Dockerfile and base image</FINDING_DETAILS>
