					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIGRef</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Web Server Security Requirements Guide :: Version 4, Release: 5 Benchmark Date: 01 Jul 2026</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>TargetKey</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA />
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIG_UUID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>24c0e41e-1385-59de-8d1a-906595a01495</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>CCI_REF</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-001849</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STATUS>NotAFinding</STATUS>
				<FINDING_DETAILS>MITIGATED. Log record storage carries a declared allocation (IR_LOGS_ALLOC_BYTES) and every health report measures bucket consumption against it, so capacity is a stated figure rather than whatever the volume happens to hold.

Evidence: backend/cases/management/commands/ship_logs.py (ALLOC_BYTES, log_storage), backend/cases/componenthealth.py (_log_storage_alerts)

Verified by: test/uat_srg_webtier.sh — the allocation is declared and reported with measured usage</FINDING_DETAILS>
