				<STATUS>Open</STATUS>
				<FINDING_DETAILS>PLANNED — requires an architectural or web-tier redesign.

Not reachable with this ingress. Refusing HTTP/1.x means not OFFERING http/1.1 in ALPN, and Traefik exposes no control over the ALPN list — its http2 settings tune streams and header tables only. Meeting this needs an ingress that can restrict ALPN, which is an ingress replacement rather than a setting. Weigh that against the exposure: HTTP/2 is negotiated and used, the only client is the workstation's managed browser, and the downgrade path is a fallback nothing on the analyst path takes.

Where: traefik/ — would require a different ingress, or an ALPN control Traefik does not have</FINDING_DETAILS>
				<COMMENTS>Determination: Redesign. Tracked in artifacts/srg_status.yml; regenerate with gen_srg_tracker.py.</COMMENTS>
				<SEVERITY_OVERRIDE />
				<SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION />
			</VULN>
