				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>CCI_REF</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-002605</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STATUS>NotAFinding</STATUS>
				<FINDING_DETAILS>MITIGATED. ci/image-currency.sh already asked the registry whether each pin had moved on; detecting drift was never the gap. The gap was that nothing recorded WHEN a review happened, so 'we check regularly' was unfalsifiable. --record writes the date AND the finding count, because a review that found five stale images and one that found none are different events; --age fails once the record passes the 30-day ceiling the control names.

Evidence: ci/image-currency.sh (--record, --age), ci/image-currency.record

Verified by: uat_srg_webtier.sh — the record exists, is within the interval, and the gate is proven to fail on an overdue record by backdating one</FINDING_DETAILS>
				<COMMENTS>Determination: Mitigated. Tracked in artifacts/srg_status.yml; regenerate with gen_srg_tracker.py.</COMMENTS>
				<SEVERITY_OVERRIDE />
				<SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION />
			</VULN>
