				<STATUS>NotAFinding</STATUS>
				<FINDING_DETAILS>MITIGATED. Keycloak passwordBlacklist(dfir-platform.txt), added to the realm password policy that converges on every deploy (D-008). The list is baked into the image beside the theme and for the same reason: a policy naming a file Keycloak cannot read fails password SETTING, and the first sign would be an analyst unable to complete a forced reset. Seeded with platform CONTEXT terms as well as weak forms — 'IrPlatform#2026' satisfies length, case, digits and specials, and is the first thing an attacker who has read the public repository would try. A composition rule cannot catch that; a list can. It gates password setting only, never sign-in.

Evidence: keycloak/password-blacklists/dfir-platform.txt, keycloak/Dockerfile (COPY + build-time test -s), hashicorp/keycloak/realm-irplatform.json passwordPolicy

Verified by: uat_srg_webtier.sh — the policy names the list, the file is present and non-empty inside the running Keycloak, and the review record is within its interval</FINDING_DETAILS>
