					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-004923</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STATUS>NotAFinding</STATUS>
				<FINDING_DETAILS>MITIGATED. Comparison against an authoritative source, with the air gap stated rather than hidden. IR_NTP_UPSTREAM names the reference and the service is disciplined by it; unset, the service serves from a LOCAL stratum 10 reference and the check reports the segment as internally consistent but NOT traceable. Stratum 10 is deliberately poor so any client that can reach a real source prefers it. CONDITIONAL BY DESIGN: a deployment that names no upstream does not satisfy traceability, and the check says so instead of passing quietly — a check that failed on the designed air-gapped case would simply be turned off.

Evidence: ntp/entrypoint.sh (upstream templating), ci/clock-sync-check.sh, deploy/.env IR_NTP_UPSTREAM

Verified by: uat_srg_webtier.sh — when IR_NTP_UPSTREAM is set the upstream must actually be reached, so an unreachable server cannot read the same as a deliberate air gap; when unset the untraceable state is reported explicitly</FINDING_DETAILS>
				<COMMENTS>Determination: Mitigated. Tracked in artifacts/srg_status.yml; regenerate with gen_srg_tracker.py.</COMMENTS>
				<SEVERITY_OVERRIDE />
				<SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION />
